{"title":"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 18","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#AMC_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">AMC 10</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A pyramid has a square base with side of length 1 and has lateral faces that are equilateral triangles. A cube is placed within the pyramid so that one face is on the base of the pyramid and its opposite face has all its edges on the lateral faces of the pyramid. What is the volume of this cube?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/6/47660cfaa8d40ad1c0cc0ae6442cda82abc8e61b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 5\\sqrt{2} - 7 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 7 - 4\\sqrt{3} \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{27} \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{9} \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"525\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can use the Pythagorean Theorem to split one of the triangular faces into two 30-60-90 triangles with side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/c/c3c585df8aa9fc1223e10f9ca9e80e8c2c8485af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}, 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"29\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/9/4e9191a5007067cff8f6d73f4d3419e08238f00b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"26\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>Next, take a cross-section of the pyramid, forming a triangle with the top of the pyramid and the midpoints of two opposite sides of the square base.\n</p><p>This triangle is isosceles with a base of 1 and two sides of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/9/4e9191a5007067cff8f6d73f4d3419e08238f00b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"26\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>The height of this triangle will equal the height of the pyramid. To find this height, split the triangle into two right triangles, with sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/4/ea482385d1d726a107500b3a8de761c6a6cbd905.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{\\sqrt2}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"48\" height=\"41\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/9/4e9191a5007067cff8f6d73f4d3419e08238f00b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"26\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>The cube, touching all four triangular faces, will form a similar pyramid that sits on top of the cube. If the cube has side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, the small pyramid has height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/c/88cc6d4aac3d9a7cfe2dd796471b38d85668e516.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"37\" height=\"41\" /> (because the pyramids are similar).\n</p><p>Thus, the height of the cube plus the height of the smaller pyramid equals the height of the larger pyramid.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/e/01e9d3e574f5c61d1281cee0d908b3c3ab7a1f87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x +\\frac{x\\sqrt{2}}{2} = \\frac{\\sqrt2}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"122\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/3/1030b0d210420b5bf06e1ba91494fb234267d58e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\left(1+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\right) =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"155\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/c/f7c49338c4e85796a0e8d611c8caf8a27eaadf28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\left(2+\\sqrt{2}\\right) = \\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"139\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/4/834d6181b1ace831b35c4a3a5c0d9e1ad8107433.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2+\\sqrt{2}}  \\cdot \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{2-\\sqrt{2}} = \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}-2}{4-2} = \\sqrt{2}-1 =$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"358\" height=\"45\" />side length of cube.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/b/57b4fd017580f77b04f4ec0cc2d5aca483ec4537.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\sqrt{2}-1\\right)^3 = (\\sqrt{2})^3 + 3(\\sqrt{2})^2(-1) + 3(\\sqrt{2})(-1)^2 + (-1)^3 = 2\\sqrt{2} - 6 +3\\sqrt{2} - 1 =\\textbf{(A)} 5\\sqrt{2} - 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"744\" height=\"35\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the side length of the square be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />. Let the top of the pyramid be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and the square base be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/a/65af420a6e2b903f5295dd8f65f321545f69e44d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCDE$\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" />. Then, let the smaller cube meet edge <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and edge <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Let the closest vertice of the cube to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> on the base of the pyramid be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />.\nConsider diagonal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/c/13c970cbf5e2e7029089517d5e8efbb8cade6d8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. It has length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/4/2c4dc1409208ff6a3039f4871d85c16763334983.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"26\" height=\"21\" />. Since the diagonal of the smaller cube's base is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/9/6798d54ee20abfb2ce2cd64969ac98c1836282eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />, note that the distance from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/7/0876d1c14c57e7b5a0bd94d502b4dfa6809f199b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2} - s\\sqrt{2}}{2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"90\" height=\"43\" /> Also, note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/d/9fdae50c9da5ac4614e447fa0f6b2e81e352361c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AG = s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/3/ff39a68f9856d8bc25688633301be9ce9fedea0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CG = 1-s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"16\" />. We can now use the Pythagorean Theorem on triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/4/1845024d637349dbc0c2899d452db2dcbf5c3f21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CHG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" />, the right angle at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, to solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />. \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/6/5e6662f33ba4ea326e705c9fd1d7e82cac25e60a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[s^2 + (\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2} - s\\sqrt{2}}{2})^2 = (1-s)^2\\]\" width=\"226\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/7/1976af1c4db60f244ec5b81736135c14ea1c7784.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\rightarrow s = \\sqrt{2} - 1 \\rightarrow \\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}}.\\]\" width=\"183\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"AMC_10\">AMC 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: AMC 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(For eventual redirection of one of the two pages.) This is also #22 on the corresponding AMC 10B.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B\">2011 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17\">Problem 17</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2011 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017042743\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.035 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.060 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 275/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2298/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6791/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.892      1 -total\n 60.26%    7.768      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 38.12%    4.914      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:9265:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017042743 and revision id 262584. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}